From: Shirogane Tsumugi <artoriapendragon123@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: axp20x_battery - allow disabling the TS pin

Boards that leave the AXP209 TS pin unconnected still get the 80uA
source driving it, so the TS ADC rails (0xfff) and the PMIC compares
that against V_LTF-charge (REG38, 2.112V by default). The result is a
permanent under-temperature fault: REG33 still reads charging-enabled,
the AC rail is up, yet the charge current stays at 0mA and the battery
reports "Not charging" forever.

Add an optional "x-powers,no-thermistor" property on the battery node
that switches the TS pin over to the generic external-ADC function
(REG84 bit 2), which takes the charge temperature comparators out of
the charging path. Boards with a real NTC fitted are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Shirogane Tsumugi <artoriapendragon123@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
@@ -37,6 +37,8 @@
 #define AXP20X_PWR_OP_BATT_PRESENT	BIT(5)
 #define AXP20X_PWR_OP_BATT_ACTIVATED	BIT(3)
 
+#define AXP20X_ADC_RATE_TS_EXT_ADC	BIT(2)
+
 #define AXP209_FG_PERCENT		GENMASK(6, 0)
 #define AXP22X_FG_VALID			BIT(7)
 
@@ -586,6 +588,18 @@
 	}
 
 	axp20x_batt->regmap = dev_get_regmap(pdev->dev.parent, NULL);
+
+	/*
+	 * Without an NTC fitted the TS pin floats to the rail, the PMIC reads
+	 * that as an under-temperature fault and silently refuses to charge.
+	 * Handing the pin to the plain ADC function takes the charge
+	 * temperature comparators out of the loop.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "x-powers,no-thermistor"))
+		regmap_update_bits(axp20x_batt->regmap, AXP20X_ADC_RATE,
+				   AXP20X_ADC_RATE_TS_EXT_ADC,
+				   AXP20X_ADC_RATE_TS_EXT_ADC);
+
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, axp20x_batt);
 
 	psy_cfg.drv_data = axp20x_batt;
